# What ships in the sdist is PUBLISHED CONTENT, so it is stated here rather than
# inherited from setuptools' default file list. That default swept the entire
# test suite (102 files) into the published 1.1.0 sdist on PyPI, which is how a
# private hostname committed to a test fixture ended up inside an artifact
# anyone can download.
#
# Deny-all, then allow. A newly added tests/, fixtures/ or scaffolding directory
# is out by construction rather than by somebody remembering to prune it - a
# deny-list only excludes the directories that existed when it was written.
#
# The cost of an allow-list is the opposite failure: a file the package NEEDS
# could be silently left out. tests/test_packaging_contents.py guards both
# directions - it builds the real sdist and wheel and asserts the sdist carries
# every package file the wheel does (so a new package-data entry cannot be
# dropped here unnoticed) BEFORE asserting no test file is present.
global-exclude *

# The build inputs a consumer needs to turn this sdist back into a wheel.
include pyproject.toml
include README.md
include LICENSE

# The package itself. Extensions are listed explicitly: a bare `graft` would
# also sweep in __pycache__ and any stray local artifact. A new package-data
# file type must be added BOTH to [tool.setuptools.package-data] and here, and
# the packaging test fails if only one of the two is done.
recursive-include src/caffeinated_whale_cli *.py
recursive-include src/caffeinated_whale_cli *.html
